\newlabel{fig:layer-sweep}{{1}{4}{PC1 $R^2$, helix $R^2$ and helix/PCA ratio plotted against layer index, for each of the four models (Latin digits 0--99). Pythia and Llama rise into the back half of the stack and stay high. Gemma-4-E4B peaks early and decays. Gemma-4-31B is nearly flat at $\sim $0.5 with a sharp spike at $L\!=\!29$ that reads as ``no helix'' if one samples at $L \!=\! 30 = N/2$}{figure.caption.5}{}}
